				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/carrington" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1555124); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1555124&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605795061" alt="Carrington" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1555124)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/carrington" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1555124); return false;" >Carrington</a></span> <span class="odate time_1583970170 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Mar 2020 23:42</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4542928">
									

<p>It's an interesting concept but a few things don't work for me. All of the below is not meant to be harsh or dismissive, I really think you have potential here and I <em>adore</em> Just Girly Things. This one just didn't work for me as well.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Stuff</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I'm not sure I understand what's going on with Dr. Chameleon; the 'color changing skin' comment makes me believe there's some backstory here, but I haven't seen it. Either way, it distracted me and muddies the waters around whatever you're trying to do with the doctor's removal from the project.</p>
<p>There's too little exploration given to how this anomaly began. They have access to -1's former home, so presumably they can piece together [i]some[/i] kind of timeline.</p>
<p>The dialogue itself could be cleaned up as well. Here are some examples:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Chameleon</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why would they be referred to in official documentation by a nickname?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5098-1, allow me to clear this up for you. You are here to be contained due to anomalous properties, and not to have your account sponsored. You will only gain access to your account as-needed for testing purposes.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is a bit torqued and difficult to follow without a close reading. It doesn't feel like natural speech. Something like &quot;SCP-5098-1, allow me to clear this up: you are in secure containment because of your anomalous nature. You're not here to have your account sponsored, and you'll only receive access to it for testing purposes.&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5098-1: An entity? What, like a ghost or something?<br />
Dr. Chameleon: That is unimportant.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It seems kind of enormously important; the nature of the entity could inform containment and analysis. It also seems a bit odd that she jumps to 'ghost or something' from 'entity'. Entity doesn't typically have supernatural connotations in every day speech. I might try something like:</p>
<p>SCP-5098-1: An entity? Uh, what do you mean<br />
Dr. Chameleon: An anomalous being, analogically similar to a ghost.<br />
SCP-5098-1: Uh, what?</p>
<p>and et cetera going into the tirade about her photographs being normal, on the back of asserting person/standard-humanhood.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Chameleon: I'd disagree. Everyone is seeing things…different. This room doesn't have pink walls, they're solid metal! It's a small room with basic furnishings. You don't have a couch, or a TV. You have long, brown hair, and you are wearing an orange Foundation sweatshirt with grey sweat pants, plus and your damn pink jacket. You don't have short pink hair. You're not wearing fishnet leggings with boots and a skirt, or whatever. I can see that! Why the fuck can't anyone else anymore?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is waaaay too much exposition from the doc, <em>plus</em> she's not wrong, what rule is she breaking? If she is affecting staff, that's a containment breach and is on the Foundation. Chameleon should probably be concerned about the fallout from that, I would think.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Chameleon: Really SCP-5098-1? Really? You don't have the right to be questioning me here.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A bit awkwardly phrased. &quot;I'm asking the questions here&quot; is cliche'd but probably better. A simple &quot;Answer the question!&quot; would be even better.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Dr. Chameleon: (Sighs) Why am I getting so worked up about this? You're the one that didn't want to believe all this! Why am I even talking to you about this? Now I'm even…acting…like…you.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yea&#8230; why are they getting so worked up? That could probably be explored, if they're gonna get worked up and call it out.</p>
<p>Final thing:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5098-1 was provided with a standard Foundation-issue smartphone with access to its Instagram account once all its followers were tracked down, amnestied, and replaced with shell accounts operated by Foundation web bots. Containment procedures have been updated to reflect this change.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>y tho?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Again, I really don't mean to trash your article and I hope you don't feel like I just vomited up a bunch of criticism. I really do think it could work with some polish. I'm no-voting for now, though.</p>

							</div>

								
